The maintainer's public halves live here, committed: tigris-release.gpg
(the GPG key that signs SHA256SUMS and the artefacts) and one .rsa.pub
a key for abuild, so mkapk.sh --release can prove the key that signed
an .apk is the maintainer's and not a throwaway. Never a private half:
a file ending in .rsa (without .pub) or a key block is refused by CI,
and the private keys live only offline with the maintainer (or, at
release time, in CI secrets). Setup, fingerprints and rotation are in
doc/release-signing.md.
